Z||000000||Fierozilla||10-26-2001||11:05 PM||||Ive gotta go to the store and buy some clear hoseing to bleed my clutch slave cylinder. What size hose (inner diameter) do I need? I cant tell by looking at it. 86 se v6 4 speed. thank you.||||reg||4
Z||000001||tgowens||10-26-2001||11:34 PM||||I'm not sure what size hose you would need but it <I>is</I> possible to bleed the clutch slave without going through all of that....... If you are doing it yourself you can open the bleeder valve slightly and just let it sit for about twenty minutes to allow any air to escape, tighten the valve, pump the pedal about three times, fill the master if needed and repeat the process. Be sure and put a small pan under the slave to catch the fluid that escapes from the slave.<P>If you have someone helping it <I>is</I> much easier though.........<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 10-26-2001).]||||reg||1
